      "slug": "67",
      "name": "67",
      "archived": false,
      "draft": false,
      "createdAt": "Sun Aug 11 2024 19:11:11 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)",
      "updatedAt": "Sun Aug 11 2024 19:11:11 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)",
      "publishedAt": "Mon Aug 12 2024 02:06:44 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)",
      "question": "<p>Define \"Liability Insurance.\"</p>",
      "answer": "<p>Insurance coverage that protects a business against claims resulting from injuries and damage to people and property.</p>",
      "type": "Law and Business"
    },
    {
      "id": "66b90ccf706977e899254b84",
      "slug": "68",
      "name": "68",
      "archived": false,
      "draft": false,
      "createdAt": "Sun Aug 11 2024 19:11:11 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)",
      "updatedAt": "Sun Aug 11 2024 19:11:11 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)",
      "publishedAt": "Mon Aug 12 2024 02:06:44 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)",
      "question": "<p>What are \"Employment Practices Liability Insurance\" (EPLI)?</p>",
      "answer": "<p>Insurance that covers businesses against claims made by employees alleging discrimination, wrongful termination, harassment, and other employment-related issues.</p>",
      "type": "Law and Business"
    },
    {
      "id": "66b90ccff8f1d06c1592f9ce",
      "slug": "69",
      "name": "69",
      "archived": false,
